More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (381–390)
381. Insecure HTTP Methods Enabled
HTTP Method Misconfiguration
Servers allow dangerous HTTP methods like PUT, DELETE, or TRACE that should be disabled.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
382. Improper Input Validation in APIs
API Input Validation Vulnerability
APIs fail to properly validate user inputs, allowing manipulation of backend logic.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
383. Publicly Accessible Log Files
Log File Exposure
Application or server logs accessible through the web reveal sensitive information.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
384. Improper Access Control in Cloud Storage
Cloud Storage Misconfiguration
Cloud storage buckets are publicly accessible and expose private data.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
385. Insecure Temporary File Handling
Temporary File Exposure
Temporary files store sensitive data and remain accessible on the server.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
386. Client-Side Authorization Enforcement
Client-Side Authorization Bypass
Authorization checks are implemented only in the frontend and can be bypassed.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $7,000
387. Unsecured Backup Database
Database Backup Exposure
Backup database files are publicly accessible from the web server.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
388. Improper Handling of Null Values
Null Value Handling Vulnerability
Applications fail to correctly process null or empty values, allowing security bypasses.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
389. Insecure Third-Party Script Loading
Third‑Party Script Injection
Applications load scripts from untrusted external sources.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
390. Exposed Internal Documentation
Internal Documentation Exposure
Internal system documentation or API documentation publicly accessible.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
